                <sc:Class>
                  <sc:name>TrafficSignalController</sc:name>
                  <sc:id>75</sc:id>
                  <sc:descriptors>
                    <sc:definition>
                      <sc:descriptorValues>
                        <sc:DescriptorValue>The TrafficSignalController provides a signal cycle to a single signal or a signal group.</sc:DescriptorValue>
                      </sc:descriptorValues>
                    </sc:definition>
                    <sc:documentation>
                      <sc:descriptorValues>
                        <sc:DescriptorValue>The TrafficSignalController provides a signal cycle to a single signal or a signal group.</sc:DescriptorValue>
                      </sc:descriptorValues>
                    </sc:documentation>
                  </sc:descriptors>
                  <sc:properties>
                    <sc:Property>
                      <sc:name>delay</sc:name>
                      <sc:id>75_594</sc:id>
                      <sc:descriptors>
                        <sc:definition>
                          <sc:descriptorValues>
                            <sc:DescriptorValue>The delay to the controller in the reference property. A controller having a delay to another one means that its first phase virtually starts delaytime seconds after the start of the reference's first phase. This can be used to define a progressive signal system, but only makes sense, if the total times of all connected controllers are the same. If delay is set, reference is required. Unit: [s]. Range: [0..inf[.</sc:DescriptorValue>
                          </sc:descriptorValues>
                        </sc:definition>
                        <sc:documentation>
                          <sc:descriptorValues>
                            <sc:DescriptorValue>The delay to the controller in the reference property. A controller having a delay to another one means that its first phase virtually starts delaytime seconds after the start of the reference's first phase. This can be used to define a progressive signal system, but only makes sense, if the total times of all connected controllers are the same. If delay is set, reference is required. Unit: [s]. Range: [0..inf[. </sc:DescriptorValue>
                          </sc:descriptorValues>
                        </sc:documentation>
                      </sc:descriptors>
                      <sc:cardinality>0..1</sc:cardinality>
                      <sc:sequenceNumber>-1073741234</sc:sequenceNumber>
                      <sc:typeName>double</sc:typeName>
                      <sc:isComposition>true</sc:isComposition>
